  for where stands come from in the first  place the sad fact is at least in the  first jojo universe you must be born  with a stand or the potential to  manifest one later in life which would  occur through profound mental strength  with that said there is also a quick and  dirty way to do it which is by being  pierced with an arrow made from an  otherworldly metal and if the person  being pierced was born with stand  potential then it will be unlocked and  if not then they will  they'll die pretty big gamble  interestingly enough having a stand  unlocked in this way  also results in a person's descendants  being able to manifest their stance if  they possess the potential which is one  of the primary catalyzing features of  jojo's bizarre adventure as we know it  meanwhile in the alternate universe  continuity of jojo these arrows  obviously don't exist and the primary  method by which stand development seems  to occur is via a mysterious shenanigan  regarding the saints corpse now as for  what kind of stance can emerge let's get  into the convoluted classification  system  which begins by being able to divide  stands into three broad types each of  which are going to have a slew of  subtypings but the original three  are ability types form types and special  types and very notably these typings are  not exclusive at any given stand will  often be distinguished by being  classified into at least two of those  broad types but this will make much more  sense as we get into it  starting with the ability typing  classification and this sector tends to  focus on allotting a stand based on the  range of its abilities so for example a  common subcategory we have here would be  a close range power type which are  generally your standard punch ghosts who  can't be more than a few meters away  from their user at any given time or i  guess they can but they become much less  effective in addition to this their  particular abilities might  be able to be used at range but they  themselves do need to stick quite close  by and a classic example of this would  be star platinum which has an effective  range of two meters from joturo and we  also have the long distance operation  types which  are stands able to operate at great  range away from their users  and a simple example of this would be  hierophant green wielded by kakyoin  what's more important to note here  though is that being a long distance  operation type  does not automatically mean that the  stan's ability is long distance  it may still be a very close range power  it can just be performed far far away  from the stan's user now these first two  sub classifications are still types of  stands that remain under the control of  their users but there are ability types  that operate on their own known as  automatic stands  which act as i said on their own under a  very simple set of commands  but they also have the distinction of  being able to act at incredible  distances away from the user however  they  are very very basic and once you figure  out effectively the one thing that the  stand is basing its decisions on then  they are usually quite easily defeated  for example killer queen sheer heart  attack ability is a far distance  autopilot type it chooses its target  based on who or whatever has the highest  temperature and very interestingly  within the world of automatic stance are  the posthumous types which either  activate or endure after their user's  death albeit with the same basic  programming as automatic stance and  notorious big from part 5 would be a  fantastic illustration of this which  attacks what it detects as the fastest  moving object within its range  and finally for ability types we also  have range irrelevant stands which  generally comprise the most terrifying  and powerful stance within the series  however the base definition of this  class are stands with abilities where  range is well like it says  irrelevant so anything that manipulates  time would be plonkier including the  world king crimson and mandam however  these stands are kind of crazy  because many of their abilities have the  potential to affect the entirety of  existence as we know it and yes i am  looking at you  made in heaven but casting ability types  aside we can also be much more  superficial and identify stands  according to their form type which  comprises five subcategories  and first up we have the common natural  humanoid stands which are exactly as it  sounds  stands which take on an organic  humanistic appearance although they  obviously don't have to mirror humanity  perfectly because things like avdol's  magician's red falls into this category  despite the fact that it does have the  head of a birdie but for a more classic  example we could turn to josuke's crazy  diamond which is effectively just a big  old dude bra  with some fairly insane powers of its  own then we move to artificial humanoid  stands which are almost the same thing  except they achieve a humanist  appearance through some sort of less  than organic construction like silver  chariot which looks like a medieval  robot or one of the stands that creeps  me out the most f13 which is cobbled  together with various non-organic matter  they would both be artificial humanoid  stands and to keep the sheer excitement  of knowledge we have going we also have  natural non-humanoid stands which i feel  like you may get the gist of by now they  are anything that takes on construction  through organic matter but does not  resemble a human appearance  and the first one of those that always  comes to mind to me is straight cat who  is a delightful cat  plant and of course to contrast that we  also have artificial non-humanoid stands  which you probably get yeah non-human  forms crafted from artificial materials  like bastet was you know  literally a powerpoint or much more  interestingly in the realm of part 8 we  have the very cool existence known as  paper moon king  but quite possibly the most exciting  subcategory of the form types are the  phenomenon stands  which basically means anything that does  not fit into the previous four  explored categories and to be clear what  that means is that it cannot manifest as  a humanoid form and it cannot be  constructed from natural or artificial  materials  so what does that leave us with well  phenomenon stands often exhibit  themselves as supernatural occurrences  or an ability granted to the user  directly say for example aktung baby  wielded by shizuka joestar which allows  her to turn herself and a select radius  around her invisible although the power  doesn't need to affect the user it can  also be applied to targets and victims  such as part 7 scary monsters which  allowed its user to infect living beings  with a virus that inevitably turned them  into dinosaurs which is it's pretty fun  for more fun though we're now going to  dive into the third broad classification  being special types and i have to note  right at the beginning  this is not an officially recognized  category in the series but more of a  framework that fans have developed over  time  spotting certain trends and i for one do  very much appreciate its existence so we  are going to dive into it here but  firstly and most boringly we have  bound stands which as the name implies  are directly tied to some form of  material or object and which also goes  on to mean that regular humans can often  see their effects actually  and the very first example of this we  saw in the series was strength which was  bound to a ship and controlled by an  orangutan because  that's jojo and it allowed said  orangutan to manipulate the ship as he  saw fit the more fun example though  would probably be superfly which was  bound to a transmission tower in mario  and had the ability to trap people  within it as well as reflect all damage  dealt to it  so something of an invincible  transmission tower moving on within the  special type we also have colony stands  which are made up of multiple conjured  beings which can range from small  handfuls like meister sex pistols or a  terrifying army of 60 patchwork soldiers  as seen in nijimora's bad company and  the main advantage of this  brand of stand is rapidly increased  utility and significantly less damage  taken  if part of your stand was to be wounded  plus if not acted one quickly these  small but powerful beings can very  swiftly overwhelm most opponents  keeping mr sex pistols in mind though  another special type is that of a  sentient stand which can obviously be  seen here as each of miesta's pistols  have their own personality  going on to interact with each other  mister and even other stand users  and in some cases sentient stands have  become exceptionally important  characters in their own right such as  foo fighters from part six who is  basically a sentient colony of plankton  that operate via a hive mind and can  infiltrate and control the bodies of  others which has led to the stone ocean  classic character foo fighters who was  aptly named directly after the stand  in addition to this the special type can  also comprise shared stands which allow  a stan to have multiple users at once or  over time an example of the latter would  be anubis from stardust crusaders who  practice the art of user hopping and fun  fact anubis would also be classified as  a sentient stand as well  and i suppose you could also call king  crimson a shared stand to some degree  as it was used by both diavolo and  doppio not really so much what we're  talking about here though finally we  also have evolving stands and these guys  are very very exciting and have resulted  in some of the most ridiculous power  that we have seen in the series but  basically this refers to stands that  have the capacity to evolve for whatever  reason such as koichi's echoes which  took on new forms based on an axe system  and each time they had different powers  and restrictions placed on them  generally becoming far stronger with  each  act but very much their own unique  existences and the stand can also go on  to evolve via that arrow thingy that we  spoke about before which when striking  user a second time can have the effect  of the original stand developing a new  sub ability which occurred in part four  when yoshikaga kira was pierced a second  time  and resulting in killer queen's absurd  bites the dust ability which can place  the targets and thus the world i guess  in a temporal loop so it's not a simple  air cool i have a new fun power to play  with this evolution process does  generally result in some pretty  world-changing stuff  and that can be seen on an even more  profound level when the stand itself is  pierced with the arrow and then it can  evolve into its requiem form which has  been seen in the series in two  incarnations one of which was silver  chariot requiem which had the power to  spot the souls of living organisms but  we also got to see it in the form of  gold experience requiem which had a  strangely esoteric power to revert  anything  back to zero which is far more  terrifying than it sounds so requiem  stands a pretty damn serious business  an evolution of a stand can also occur  through a mysterious process hinted at  but not technically detailed in part six  whereby it involves the fusing of souls  with a stand user and crafting specific  gravitational requirements which yeah i  know  sounds very obscure but it did result in  the insanity that is made in heaven so  yeah in conclusion stand evolution is  madness and that is our three broad  typings and their subcategories  so in theory with this information  equipped we should be able to identify  and classify any stand  and in fact let's just test that out  right now let's take moody blues for  example and now we know that we could  classify that as a close range  artificial humanoid stand oh  don't we all feel smart now one last  thing though all stands in the series  are further dissected through a  parameter system that measures the six  key classes of statistics those being  destructive power  speed range persistence precision and  development potential with each state  being assigned a rank from a to e  and it generally provides us with a nice  solid visual cheat sheet of a stan's  general strength and weaknesses one that  we will apply going forward in this  encyclopedia  although they are quite inconsistent so  just a  warning there and that does pretty much  do it for this prologue to the stand  encyclopedia and i suppose next time we  will be picking up with our first  official entry which is going to be star  platinum  wielded by the one and only joe turokujo  so yeah we'll see how that goes i'm  honestly pretty nervous about this whole  idea because jojo views on this channel  are hard enough to come by as it is but  we're going to give it a go  anyway but what do you guys think please  do let me know down in the comments  below and if you are keen for some more  jojo content then please do go and check  out some of my other videos or even  subscribe to the channel for regular  jojo wonder delivered straight into your  youtube feed but for now this has been  the new world review  and i'll see you next time

